  "summary": "A visual style characterized by the intentional use of Bayer matrix dithering patterns to create the illusion of color depth in limited-color displays.",
  "description": "It appears as a repeating grid of dots that vary in size to simulate grayscale or color transitions, resulting in a distinctive crosshatch pattern. This emerged from technical constraints in early digital imaging where limited palettes required mathematical dithering algorithms to approximate continuous tones.",
